      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i was just digging through the latest mainnet release of the protocol's core library. i noticed the implementation of the point-addition formula in the custom birational equivalence layer is still using that exact same non-standard coefficient set i pushed to the private testnet before the foundation pulled my credentials.\n\nit's such a niche way to optimize the scalar multiplication for that specific curve, and it's definitely not the standard way the 'official' docs say it should be done. can you check if that specific coefficient set is still active in the current production binary? if they're still running my exact optimization while claiming it's their own research, i've got them dead to rights.",
